			<div class="content" id="post-content-1544662">
									

<p>The tone is terrible, so many non-clinical turns of phrase that I can't even list them all.</p>
<p>But the writing and execution are just so damn good that I don't care. I love the way you've thought of al lteh different angles. What happens if wearer says somethign impossible? What happens if two statemetns cotnradict? What happens if there is a language barrier? I particularly like that the wearer isn't immune. Reminds me of my favorite anomalous item, a spear that seeks out the nearest living thing, and not neccesarily nearest down-range.</p>
<p>That last note left me gobsmacked. The effected are utterly incapable of realizing that they are deluded. Reality is no longer objectively verifiable. That is the most existentially scary thing I think I have ever read.</p>
<p>I don't have enough +1s.</p>

