			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1544723">
									

<p>Thank you for taking the time to critique this, I really appreciate it. I do disagree about the containment procedures needing to specify non-destructive testing &#8212; as all tests must be authorized by The Powers That Be, I personally don't think it matters if every mook reading the report knows what sorts of tests are going to be approved and which are going to be denied. Following the containment procedures as written will result in no destructive testing being performed, because such tests will be denied authorization. I have nonetheless reworded the offending sentence and hopefully it reads better now.</p>
<p>Most of the rest I'm going to leave alone for right now so I can sleep on it. As you say, I don't want to strive so hard for a dry clinical presentation that I lose the overall feeling.</p>

